BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:JOIN US FOR AN AUTHOR SOCIAL WITH THERESA SHEA & ERUM SHAZIA HASAN
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261013T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261013T203000
UID:bm-6497720261013@flyingbooks.ca
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://cdn1.bookmanager.com/i/8102716/ECW.png?c
 b=1790972756
DESCRIPTION:[Author Social]\nJoin author Theresa Shea in conversation with
  Erum Shazia Hasan for an Author Social!\nFor fans of Claire Keegan’s\nS
 mall Things Like These\nand Karen Joy Fowler’s\nWe Are All Completely Be
 side Ourselves\n\,\nDog Days of Planet Earth\ni\ns an unforgettable and fi
 ercely compassionate novel. Weaving together major environmental and polit
 ical issues of the mid- to late-20th century that remain urgent today\, th
 e novel asks what we’re willing to risk for our personal convictions in 
 a world where powerful and unjust forces often oppose them.\nFree to atten
 d\, but we have limited spots -  please\nRSVP HERE\n.\nTheresa Shea is th
 e author of two previous novels. Her debut\,\nThe Unfinished Child\,\nwas 
 a finalist for the 2014 Alberta Book Award and the Alberta Readers’ Choi
 ce Award. Her second novel\,\nThe Shade Tree\,\nwon the 2020 Guernica Priz
 e and the 2022 Alberta Book Award. Shea lives and writes in Edmonton\, AB.
 \nErum Shazia Hasan is the bestselling author of\nWe Meant Well\,\nwhich w
 as longlisted for the 2023 Giller Prize. Born in Canada and raised in Fran
 ce\, Hasan now lives in Toronto and works as a sustainable development con
 sultant with the United Nations and other international agencies. Her writ
 ing explores questions of identity\, culture and belonging across borders.
LOCATION:Flying Books at Neverland\, 371 Queen St. W.
URL:https://flyingbooks.ca/events
X-SOURCE:Flying Books
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:JOIN US FOR THE LAUNCH OF CANTALOUPE
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261014T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261014T200000
UID:bm-6181520261014@flyingbooks.ca
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://cdn1.bookmanager.com/i/8102716/cantaloup
 e.png?cb=1791402226
DESCRIPTION:[Book Launch]\nJoin Flying Books and Freehand Books for the To
 ronto launch of\nCantaloupe!\nby M. Jay Smith in conversation with Lucian 
 Childs\, author of\nConfluence.\nCantaloupe!\nbrings us nine juicy stories
  about trying (and failing) to do the right thing — about\ncharacters wh
 o strive to hold everything together while staying true to their convictio
 ns and sense of\njustice in the process. With razor-sharp prose and a bit 
 of slapstick humour\, M. Jay Smith contemplates\nhow identities smudge int
 o each other\, how they shout and push and wither and explode under\npress
 ure. And no matter what\, one’s best intentions go a little bit awry.\n
 “M. Jay Smith writes with rare honesty about ordinary people.— Peter 
 Midgley\, author of Let Us Not\nThink of Them As Barbarians\n“M. Jay Sm
 ith’s wry stories surprise at every turn to wondrously reveal the anguis
 h and exhilaration\nrunning through our faltering\, fluttering human heart
 s.” — Mikka Jacobsen\, author of Good Victory
LOCATION:Flying Books\, 784 College Street
URL:https://flyingbooks.ca/events
X-SOURCE:Flying Books
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:JOIN US FOR AN AUTHOR SOCIAL WITH IAIN REID AND ELLIE FOUMBI
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261014T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261014T203000
UID:bm-6464520261014@flyingbooks.ca
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://cdn1.bookmanager.com/i/8102716/Iain_and_
 Ellie.png?cb=1790628544
DESCRIPTION:[Author Social]\nJoin Iain Reid and Ellie Foumbi as they discu
 ss their haunting\, philosophical new novel\,\nA New Kind of Clean\n\, a c
 ollaboration from the author of\nFoe\nand\nI'm Thinking of Ending Things\n
 and the filmmaker of\nOur Father\, the Devil\nand the upcoming\nFleur.\nFr
 ee to attend\, but we have limited spots -  please\nRSVP HERE\n.\nMissy D
 jalo has spent years trying to become a real working actor\, someone who b
 elongs in the spotlight\, but her life so far has been failed auditions\, 
 sleepless nights running monologues\, and watching prettier\, better-conne
 cted actresses get chosen over her. When she's invited to audition for a l
 ucrative commercial\, it feels like her big break. But as the audition str
 etches on\, reality and fantasy blur\, and Missy begins to wonder what she
 'll have to sacrifice to get there. Brimming with unease until the last pa
 ge\, A New Kind of Clean is a surreal\, minimalist fable about memory\, am
 bition\, and reality from two acclaimed masters of their craft.\nIain Reid
  has written five books\, including the\nNew York Times\nbestselling novel
  I\n’m Thinking of Ending Thing\ns\, which has been translated into more
  than twenty languages and was adapted into a Netflix film by Oscar winner
  Charlie Kaufman. His second novel\,\nFoe\,\nwas also adapted to film\, st
 arring Saoirse Ronan and Paul Mescal. His third novel\,\nWe Spread\n\, was
  nominated for the Governor General’s Literary Award.\nEllie Foumbi is a
 n award-winning screenwriter and director. She was born in Cameroon and gr
 ew up in Westchester\, New York. After completing an MFA at Columbia Unive
 rsity’s School of the Arts\, she made her debut feature film\,\nOur Fath
 er\, the Devil\,\nwhich premiered at the Venice Film Festival and received
  universal critical acclaim. She was named one of 25 New Faces of Independ
 ent Film by Filmmaker Magazine. Ellie’s work is focused on unique\, char
 acter-driven stories that explore pressing cultural and social-political i
 ssues through a genre lens.
LOCATION:Flying Books at Neverland\, 371 Queen St. W.
URL:https://flyingbooks.ca/events
X-SOURCE:Flying Books
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:JOIN US FOR OUR OCTOBER FICTION BOOK CLUB
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261019T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261020T203000
UID:bm-6345920261019@flyingbooks.ca
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://cdn1.bookmanager.com/i/8102716/Oct_Fic_B
 C_2026.jpg?cb=1789164902
DESCRIPTION:[Book Club]\nFrom the Booker Prize–winning author of\nA Brie
 f History of Seven Killings\n\, Marlon James is back with another longlist
 ed title.\nIn\nThe Disappearers\n\, James has written a riveting and deepl
 y human story of men forced to make compromises to survive that the societ
 y they live in demands. It is both a dramatic page-turner and an unflinchi
 ng exploration of queer life in Jamaica during the 1980s and 1990s.\nJoin 
 us on Monday\, October 19th and Tuesday\, October 20th for a thrilling con
 versation. We hope to see you there.\nYour book club ticket includes:\nA g
 lass of wine (or another beverage of your choice).\nA thoughtful conversat
 ion with our brilliant moderator\, Lee Suksi.\nA $20 credit toward any boo
 k in the shop.*\nGET YOUR TICKETS HERE!\nA few details:\nTicket price incl
 udes HST and fees.\n*$20 book credit is valid on the night of attendance o
 nly (non-refundable and non-transferable).\nWine is served on the night of
  the event (ID required).\nTickets are non-refundable within 7 days of the
  event\; due to limited capacity and planning\, we’re not able to transf
 er tickets to future book club sessions.
LOCATION:Flying Books at Neverland\, 371 Queen St. W.
URL:https://flyingbooks.ca/events
X-SOURCE:Flying Books
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:JOIN US FOR THE LAUNCH OF YOU KNOW WHAT YOU DID: THE HILLS
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261022T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261022T200000
UID:bm-6198920261022@flyingbooks.ca
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://cdn1.bookmanager.com/i/8102716/YOU_KNOW_
 WHAT_YOU_DID___flying_books___corrected.png?cb=1790884216
DESCRIPTION:[Book Launch]\nJoin Flying Books and ECW Press to celebrate th
 e Toronto launch of\nYou Know What You Did: The Hills\nby Lisa Whittington
 -Hill in conversation with Anne T. Donahue. Admission is free\, but space
  is limited. Please\nRSVP\nto attend.\nMarking 20th anniversary of The Hil
 ls\,\nYou Know What You Did\ndelivers a funny and generous look at reality
  television’s most influential docusoap\, starring the infamous Lauren C
 onrad\, and how it changed the conversation on fame. With a healthy dose o
 f cynicism and empathy for the chaos of the Hollywood maelstrom\,\nYou Kno
 w What You Did\nshows us the lasting impact that The Hills had on everythi
 ng we know about celebrity\, reality\, and young womanhood — covering ho
 t topics like the Kardashians\, Real Housewives\, and more!\nA certified p
 op culture expert\, Lisa Whittington-Hill is the author of\nGirls\, Interr
 upted: How Pop Culture Is Failing Women\nand\nThe Go-Go’s Beauty and the
  Beat\n. Her work has appeared in\nLongreads\, The Walrus\, Hazlitt\, Cata
 pult\n\, and she is the publisher of\nThis Magazine\n. Lisa lives in Toron
 to\, ON.
LOCATION:Flying Books\, 784 College Street
URL:https://flyingbooks.ca/events
X-SOURCE:Flying Books
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:MAKE IT MAKE SENSE: THE FLYING BOOKS NONFICTION BOOKCLUB
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261025T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261025T203000
UID:bm-6443520261025@flyingbooks.ca
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://cdn1.bookmanager.com/i/8102716/Oct_Nonfi
 c_Book_Club_2026.jpg?cb=1790375582
DESCRIPTION:[Book Club]\nJoin Tomas Hachard\, author of\nCity in Flames\n\
 , on Sunday\, October 25th\, from 6:30 to 8:30 pm for a lively discussion 
 of\nThe Reverse Centaur’s Guide to Life After AI\nby Cory Doctorow.\nA s
 hort\, provocative guide to what's good\, bad\, and stupid about AI and th
 e discourse around AI\, by the author of\nEnshittification\n.\nThe Reverse
  Centaur’s Guide to Life After AI\nis not another anti-AI screed. Cory D
 octorow uses AI in his work every day. As a creative person\, he has no mo
 ral or dogmatic issue with it—he thinks the technology is useful\, even 
 exciting\, and full of potential. And yet.\nFor Doctorow\, it is imperativ
 e to see through the hype to the real story\, to understand the technology
  not just for what it does\, but for who it does it to and who for. Doctor
 ow recounts both how we found ourselves in this dire situation and how we 
 can get through it\, to a life “after” AI in which the tools work for 
 us\, not the other way around.\nJoin us on Sunday\, October 25th for an ev
 ening of conversation. We hope to see you there.\nGET YOUR TICKETS HERE!\n
 Your book club ticket includes:\nA glass of wine (or another beverage of y
 our choice).\nA thoughtful conversation with Tomas Hachard\, author of\nCi
 ty in Flames\n.\nA $20 credit toward any book in the shop.\nA few details:
 \nTicket price includes HST and fees.\n$20 book credit is valid on the nig
 ht of attendance only (non-refundable and non-transferable).\nWine is serv
 ed on the night of the event (ID required).\nTickets are non-refundable wi
 thin 7 days of the event\; due to limited capacity and planning\, we’re 
 not able to transfer tickets to future book club sessions.
LOCATION:Flying Books at Neverland\, 371 Queen St. W.
URL:https://flyingbooks.ca/events
X-SOURCE:Flying Books
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:TIFA Presents Ann Cleeves
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261026T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261026T203000
UID:bm-6544720261026@flyingbooks.ca
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://cdn1.bookmanager.com/i/8102716/Ann_Cleev
 es.png?cb=1791461782
DESCRIPTION:[Book Launch]\nToronto Festival of Authors presents internatio
 nally bestselling author Ann Cleeves as she discusses the latest installme
 nt of her gripping Two Rivers series\,\nThe Dying Light\n.\nDetective Matt
 hew Venn must solve a mysterious death in a luxury holiday home while caug
 ht between a powerful family’s secrets and a powder keg of local tension
 s.\nAnn Cleeves is the bestselling author of more than thirty-five critica
 lly acclaimed novels\, and in 2017 was awarded the highest accolade in cri
 me writing\, the CWA Diamond Dagger. She is the creator of popular detecti
 ves Vera Stanhope\, Jimmy Perez\, and Matthew Venn\, who can be found on t
 elevision’s\nVera\,\nShetland\n\, and\nThe Long Call\n. The TV series an
 d the books they are based on have become international sensations\, captu
 ring the minds of millions worldwide.\nTickets on Sale Now!\n👉\n\nBooks
  will be available for purchase on site courtesy of @flyingbooks_to
LOCATION:Isabel Bader Theatre\, 93 Charles St West\, Toronto\, ON
URL:https://flyingbooks.ca/events
X-SOURCE:Flying Books
